{
  "dom_id": "step-q97631",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "A particle moves along a circular path centered at $O$ in the $xy$-plane in the counterclockwise direction with a constant angular velocity of $1\\text{\u00a0rad/s}.$ Given that the object is at the position $(4,0)$ when $t=0,$ find the position function of the particle.",
  "worked_solution": "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and the particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nSince the object's initial position is $(4,0),$ we have that $r(0)=4i,$ and we can conclude that the circle's radius is $R=4.$\n\nTherefore, since we have $R=4$ and $\\omega =1\\text{\u00a0rad/s},$ we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =4(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
